{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqiwte4ddob","workspace":"D:/zonoid","title":"FeatureBench auth via CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is supported — FB-4 worker conclusion was wrong","summary":"The FB-4 worker concluded that FeatureBench's claude_code agent cannot forward CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN to Docker containers and only exports ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. This is INCORRECT. The get_env_setup_script() in claude_code.py has a catch-all loop: `for key, value in self.env_vars.items(): if key not in required_vars and value: required_vars[key] = value` which forwards ANY env var from self.env_vars (populated from config.toml [env]) into the container. CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is not in required_vars, so it falls through the loop and gets exported. The fix: add CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN to the [env] section of a gitignored .fb-infer-config.toml (pattern .fb-infer-config*.toml already in .gitignore). The claude CLI inside the container picks up CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN natively. Token is already in .env.local — generate .fb-infer-config.toml from it before running fb infer.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-18T02:57:41.053Z","vec":[-0.01211910042911768,0.04412231966853142,-0.08165135979652405,-0.029598060995340347,0.04004501551389694,-0.05065155029296875,0.056418586522340775,0.05056868866086006,-0.06985988467931747,-0.015583719126880169,-0.03845290467143059,-0.09817484766244888,0.019684791564941406,-0.020001940429210663,0.06564630568027496,0.05138566344976425,0.06772925704717636,-0.011419208720326424,-0.02205023169517517,0.03654753044247627,-0.10207240283489227,-0.023997077718377113,0.02885335311293602,0.013012060895562172,-0.02049020119011402,-0.1134287640452385,-0.058734532445669174,-0.04892909154295921,0.020728429779410362,0.047532275319099426,0.06310353428125381,0.10853178054094315,-0.060181982815265656,0.027500320225954056,0.15340007841587067,0.09558075666427612,0.05059164762496948,-0.07626062631607056,-0.06774334609508514,0.022626638412475586,0.03920670598745346,0.02227614633